spans.s:
कंस॑ m. a vessel made of metal;
 metal, brass (also n.);
 N.
of a myth. king slain by Kṛṣṇa.

कन् (only pp. का॑यमान, aor. अकानिषम्, & perf. or
intens-stem चाकन् or चकान्) be glad, be satisfied with, enjoy (acc.,
loc., gen., or instr.);
 be liked, please, (w. gen.);
 love, wish, desire
(acc.). — आ be pleased with (loc.);
 strive after, long for. — Cf.
संचकान॑.

कनिष्ठक^1 f. ˚ष्ठिका॑ the smallest;
 f. कनि॑ष्ठिका
the little finger;
 subordination, obedience.
[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160315. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/252.

क॑नीयंस् (compar.) smaller, less, younger, very little
or small;
 m. a younger son or brother.

कन्य a. the smallest;
 f. कन्या॑ girl, maid, daughter, the
Virgo in the zodiac.

कानन n. forest;
 ˚नान्त n. region of the f.;
 ˚नौकस्
m. ape (inhabitant of the f.).

कान्त a. desired, loved, lovely, beautiful. m. the beloved
man, husband;
 f. beloved or lovely woman, mistress, wife.
